Subject: [PATCH 2/4] chore(lint): CLAUDE.md's rules as errors, layered
 imports, an import-cycle test; dead code and unused exports gone
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

eslint.config.mjs: every CLAUDE.md rule at error (one export per .tsx, named types in types.ts,
React's hook rules with the compiler's diagnostics, import/no-cycle, cognitive complexity 15,
ts-expect-error with a description), unused directives an error, unicorn/no-useless-undefined
and camelcase with their reasons (decisions Q2, §0.6.7); the tests' TSX_TYPE off, and three hook
rules off for the eight suites that hold fact 31's findings, named by file. The 7 old zones give
way to the layered ones of §1.7.4, with two file-scoped exceptions (header-account and its test
read src/lib/session; the note scanner's test reads the server's showdown options). Each zone was
probed with eslint's lintText (35 probes, nothing written). The node kit's no-null directive and
its config block go together (amendment 2 (b)); 98 directives the new options made unused go.
src/__tests__/import-cycles.test.ts holds the graph, type-only imports included, at no cycle.

Phase 4 items: useToastSetting, useToastTop and useFavorites in their own files; gmRollsOf to
FR/utils/gm-rolls (NO_GM_ROLLS to FR/constants); SpellSlotPool, RollBrief, Creature, RollToast,
ToastBook, ChoiceProblem to their types.ts, with ToastDraft and WayWords named; TOAST_FOR and
COOKBOOK_MOST_DELAY to constants; SocialProviderId a literal union in src/types/auth.ts that the
providers' object is checked against; LastHeard in last-heard.tsx; the HIT_DIE test beside its
constant; usePopover's onOpenChange typed as floating-ui's. useFollow and `due` stay (G-12, G-13).
Relative imports that leave their feature or top folder now use @/ paths (77, import lines only).
Dead code: jest.setup's mockFetch and mockManyFetch, useWildShaping and two unused types; 44
exports used only in their own module lose `export` (no Next.js special file, no 'use server'
module). React-hooks findings: use-draft-focus reads its mount-time values from its ref; the six
left in notes' hooks are timing-bound and keep line disables with reasons (13 react-hooks, 34 in
all).

L1 (APP's tools, before the allowances landed): jest 318 suites, 9,727 tests, 0 red; tsc 0
errors; eslint 1,161 files, 0 errors, 0 warnings; gates 1-9 and 12 ok (0 cycle groups); gates 10
and 11 FAIL on exactly the two lines the previous commit's allowances name, and ok with them.

